  "body": "Description:\r\n> I have an invite from an IRC user (global on snoonet) but when i try to accept or decline it gives me an error: Room '!HaEJfkIQMGuDbPkiAh:matrix.org' does not exist\r\n\r\nThe matrix user was over federation:\r\n - `@jack:jack-server.com`\r\n - `@_snoonet_Global:matrix.org`\r\n\r\nRemote HS logs:\r\n```\r\nhomeserver.log.2:2017-02-03 21:33:01,106 - synapse.http.server - 123 - INFO - POST-1069327- <SynapseRequest at 0xfb04998 method=POST uri=/_matrix/client/r0/join/%21HaEJfkIQMGuDbPkiAh%3Amatrix.org?access_token=<redacted> clientproto=HTTP/1.1 site=8448> SynapseError: 403 - Room '!HaEJfkIQMGuDbPkiAh:matrix.org' does not exist\r\n```\r\n\r\nInvestigation:\r\n> that room was created on Wed 2016-12-21 03:52:34 UTC (~2 months ago)\r\nyou were last invited to that room on Fri 2017-02-03 12:04:42 UTC (3 days ago)\r\nit looks like you did interact with that room previously: there is a replaces_state entry for your m.room.member event with the event ID $148362919587XAfQu:jack-server.com\r\n\r\nGiven this, and the fact that there is an event ID sent from your server, tells me that your server has forgotten about this room. I don't know why.",
